# envhub config — copy this to ~/.config/envhub/config and edit it.
# Everything here is optional; with no config at all, envhub searches your
# whole home folder.

# A plain path = a folder to search for .env files in.
# List one per line to search only those folders (faster, less noise):
#
#   ~/code
#   ~/work/backend

# A line starting with ! = a folder name to ignore, wherever it appears.
# node_modules, .git, Library, target, .venv, .cache and friends are already
# ignored, so you only need this for your own noise:
#
#   !dist
#   !backup
